WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.755 --> 00:00:12.551
You don't hear much praise for China
in the United States these days.

00:00:12.592 --> 00:00:15.720
To be fair, China doesn't say
great things about the US either.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:16.721
(Laughter)

00:00:16.721 --> 00:00:20.725
The two big nations are stuck
in a geopolitical deadlock

00:00:20.767 --> 00:00:24.855
that is bad for progress
to fight climate change.

00:00:24.896 --> 00:00:27.774
I'm a China sustainability policy analyst

00:00:27.816 --> 00:00:31.528
and I have witnessed
a clean energy revolution there

00:00:31.528 --> 00:00:35.115
that could mean big things
for the rest of the world.

00:00:35.115 --> 00:00:37.284
But it's become clear to me

00:00:37.284 --> 00:00:41.204
that if the US continues
to see China as a threat,

00:00:41.204 --> 00:00:46.293
the desired transition
will never happen at the faster pace

00:00:46.293 --> 00:00:48.837
and the larger scale as expected.

00:00:49.504 --> 00:00:55.010
We urgently need to pivot
from the currently dismal relations

00:00:55.051 --> 00:00:59.347
and reset a constructive
rather than destructive foundation

00:00:59.389 --> 00:01:01.683
for a global clean energy revolution.

00:01:02.183 --> 00:01:08.106
(Applause)

00:01:09.024 --> 00:01:14.279
Let's take a look
at the clean energy manufacturing,

00:01:14.279 --> 00:01:17.407
because this seems to be
where the tension lies today.

00:01:18.533 --> 00:01:20.869
Some US commentators said,

00:01:20.869 --> 00:01:25.790
"The best chance was 10 years ago.
The second best chance is now."

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:27.834
The best chance was China's drive

00:01:27.834 --> 00:01:32.088
to invest aggressively and ambitiously
in clean technologies

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:34.591
with the China Make 2025 campaign.

00:01:35.717 --> 00:01:40.639
The outcome is massive deployment
of clean energy solutions

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:44.809
that established China
as a global leader in this landscape.

00:01:45.769 --> 00:01:50.065
The US Inflation Reduction Act in 2022,

00:01:50.106 --> 00:01:56.112
a climate law that pushes for investments
in domestic clean energy production,

00:01:56.112 --> 00:01:59.199
represents the second best chance.

00:01:59.199 --> 00:02:04.120
The IEA executive director Fatih
vividly called this dynamic

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:08.375
“the beginning of a new age
of clean energy manufacturing.”

00:02:09.584 --> 00:02:14.255
A decade apart, China and the US
stand at a different position

00:02:14.297 --> 00:02:16.049
along the global value chain.

00:02:16.633 --> 00:02:20.679
While China is already
in the second decade of transition,

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:23.223
the US is just starting to take off.

00:02:24.265 --> 00:02:30.397
The recent data shows China provided
77 percent of global batteries last year

00:02:30.438 --> 00:02:33.775
and it is right on track
to lead all nations

00:02:33.775 --> 00:02:38.029
in manufacturing
clean energy products by 2030.

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:42.784
China's investment
has also put it as a global leader,

00:02:42.784 --> 00:02:47.706
leading exporter of those technologies:
solar, wind, batteries,

00:02:47.706 --> 00:02:48.873
you name it.

00:02:49.666 --> 00:02:52.252
My professional experience also tells me

00:02:52.293 --> 00:02:57.674
that the US can learn a great deal
from China's steadfast dedication

00:02:57.716 --> 00:03:02.512
to push forward the clean energy
transition in some key ways.

00:03:03.179 --> 00:03:07.642
Firstly, China is re-energizing
the world's largest energy system

00:03:07.684 --> 00:03:10.895
with renewables
and smart grid infrastructure.

00:03:10.937 --> 00:03:15.233
And the US can adapt this
with a much shorter learning curve

00:03:15.233 --> 00:03:16.776
and reduced costs.

00:03:17.527 --> 00:03:22.198
The first half of this year
saw 34 percent of China’s electricity

00:03:22.198 --> 00:03:24.659
generated from non-fossil fuels,

00:03:24.659 --> 00:03:29.539
right on track to deliver 
39 percent by 2025,

00:03:29.539 --> 00:03:31.041
as has been planned,

00:03:31.041 --> 00:03:34.794
and aiming for 80 percent by 2035.

00:03:34.836 --> 00:03:37.213
Between now and 2035,

00:03:37.255 --> 00:03:43.094
China's national endeavors are focused
on rapid expansion of installations

00:03:43.136 --> 00:03:48.349
and also consumption of clean energy
in all sectors you could imagine.

00:03:48.391 --> 00:03:49.642
In the meantime,

00:03:49.684 --> 00:03:55.565
it's also dedicated to enhancing
grid transmission and distribution systems

00:03:55.607 --> 00:03:58.234
to accommodate this growth of renewables.

00:03:59.903 --> 00:04:05.700
US and China operate power systems
in two different regulatory contexts,

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:09.120
but share the logic and also technicality

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:11.414
when designing and building

00:04:11.414 --> 00:04:16.252
a clean, smart, net-zero
carbon emissions grid system.

00:04:16.294 --> 00:04:20.298
China is also becoming a real daredevil

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:23.134
in pioneering the development of 5G

00:04:23.176 --> 00:04:26.346
and AI-enabled power systems

00:04:26.387 --> 00:04:32.685
and deploying the
ultra-high-voltage grid systems

00:04:32.727 --> 00:04:37.398
supplemented by
vehicle-to-grid technologies

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:40.318
in order to accommodate the rise of EVs.

00:04:41.194 --> 00:04:46.449
China's experience can provide
an invaluable reference or insight

00:04:46.449 --> 00:04:50.286
for the US to decarbonize
your own power system.

00:04:51.371 --> 00:04:54.791
Secondly, China is leading
a global campaign

00:04:54.791 --> 00:04:57.585
to increase solar usage.

00:04:57.627 --> 00:05:02.048
The social, economic and environmental
model deployed in China

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:06.636
can help the US to address
climate injustice challenges domestically.

00:05:07.679 --> 00:05:11.516
Solar energy is becoming
the least-cost option

00:05:11.558 --> 00:05:15.353
for new electricity generation
in most parts of the world today.

00:05:15.395 --> 00:05:20.024
The IEA forecasts an average annual
solar generation growth

00:05:20.066 --> 00:05:24.362
of 25 percent between 2022 and 2030,

00:05:24.362 --> 00:05:29.284
which is about 10 times
of the current total global installations,

00:05:29.284 --> 00:05:33.121
in order to achieve net-zero
carbon emissions by mid-century.

00:05:34.372 --> 00:05:36.082
Or to put it another way,

00:05:36.082 --> 00:05:42.505
this is one kilowatt
solar installation per person by 2030.

00:05:42.547 --> 00:05:47.844
That number stands today
at one-tenth kilowatt globally.

00:05:48.845 --> 00:05:52.473
China is on its way
to achieve two-fifths kilowatt

00:05:52.515 --> 00:05:54.225
by the end of this year.

00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:59.731
To bridge the gap, a group of leading
Chinese universities and institutions

00:05:59.772 --> 00:06:01.399
launched a China campaign

00:06:01.441 --> 00:06:07.030
advocating one kilowatt
solar installation per person by 2030.

00:06:08.823 --> 00:06:12.785
The strategy is -- and also
turning that into a global campaign,

00:06:12.785 --> 00:06:15.038
called Solar Lights the Planet.

00:06:15.038 --> 00:06:18.499
The strategy is to really use
solar installation

00:06:18.499 --> 00:06:20.126
as the intervention point

00:06:20.168 --> 00:06:24.214
to explore how rural
energy transition in China

00:06:24.255 --> 00:06:27.884
can benefit other
UN sustainability targets.

00:06:29.135 --> 00:06:32.597
On one side, it's cost-effective.

00:06:32.639 --> 00:06:38.353
One kilowatt solar installation
requires five square meters of space

00:06:38.394 --> 00:06:41.940
and a 500-dollar
upfront investment to install.

00:06:43.149 --> 00:06:46.027
When completed,
it generates green electricity

00:06:46.027 --> 00:06:47.779
while avoiding carbon emissions.

00:06:49.489 --> 00:06:50.949
And on the other side,

00:06:50.949 --> 00:06:56.788
it also demonstrates that co-benefits
can be created and maximized.

00:06:58.248 --> 00:07:03.211
Rapid rural energy transition
can bring new investment

00:07:03.253 --> 00:07:07.465
and also create green power-enabled
growth opportunities,

00:07:07.507 --> 00:07:12.387
for instance, food, agriculture,
fishery, energy services,

00:07:12.428 --> 00:07:14.847
tourism and other industries.

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:20.853
China's experience definitely
can be very valuable for the US

00:07:20.895 --> 00:07:24.691
to think about the solutions
to address climate injustice.

00:07:25.692 --> 00:07:28.778
Solar Lights The Planet is the ambition.

00:07:28.778 --> 00:07:31.906
It also offers colleagues
in the United States

00:07:31.906 --> 00:07:36.160
to work with peers from China
and other parts of the world

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:40.248
to really tackle
the climate injustice challenge.

00:07:41.499 --> 00:07:45.670
Thirdly, China is mainstreaming
a circular economy

00:07:45.712 --> 00:07:48.881
and transforming its supply chains.

00:07:48.923 --> 00:07:53.052
Joining forces, China,
the US, together with the EU,

00:07:53.094 --> 00:07:58.725
can literally reset the global
supply chain solidly on sustainability.

00:08:00.435 --> 00:08:03.980
China is a global
manufacturing powerhouse.

00:08:04.022 --> 00:08:06.107
Its demand for raw materials

00:08:06.149 --> 00:08:10.153
and critical metals
is growing exponentially.

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:15.241
As we all know, the planet
cannot possibly afford

00:08:15.241 --> 00:08:18.328
the ecological destruction from quadruple,

00:08:18.328 --> 00:08:23.458
and in some cases even six times
the current import of critical metals

00:08:23.458 --> 00:08:26.044
to match the planned energy transition.

00:08:27.128 --> 00:08:32.967
A circular economy offers a remedy
to decouple the growth from resource use.

00:08:33.968 --> 00:08:38.348
China is also well positioned
to reset its supply chains

00:08:38.389 --> 00:08:40.433
with circularity at the core.

00:08:41.642 --> 00:08:46.147
Today, China recycles more than
95 percent of nickel and lithium.

00:08:46.731 --> 00:08:49.650
Business communities
have a big role to play,

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:53.988
providing solutions or answers
to what hurdles to remove,

00:08:53.988 --> 00:08:56.532
what innovative solutions to deploy,

00:08:56.532 --> 00:08:58.701
what business models actually to promote,

00:08:58.701 --> 00:09:03.122
and very importantly,
how to consolidate a global partnership

00:09:03.122 --> 00:09:08.878
to work together to shape our sustainable
and circular global supply chain.

00:09:09.754 --> 00:09:14.342
Which is why a group of Chinese
organizations are working together,

00:09:14.384 --> 00:09:18.262
kicking off a China
Circularity 100 initiative,

00:09:18.304 --> 00:09:22.141
aiming by 2030 to really find the pathways

00:09:22.183 --> 00:09:25.978
to close the loop in recycling
for critical metals

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:28.856
and also for the energy sector.

00:09:28.898 --> 00:09:31.401
It's targeting at least 100 companies

00:09:31.401 --> 00:09:35.029
to work together
to find the alternative pathways.

00:09:36.948 --> 00:09:40.785
China's practice can become
a very important reference

00:09:40.785 --> 00:09:44.080
for the United States
to make investment decisions

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:47.166
to embrace circularity now.

00:09:48.543 --> 00:09:54.090
So how do we jump-start
a new US-China partnership?

00:09:54.132 --> 00:10:00.555
Well, the two governments ...
should start with a revised narrative,

00:10:00.596 --> 00:10:07.520
one that is with good intention,
as well as with collaborative spirit.

00:10:08.771 --> 00:10:12.567
In the meantime, the two nations
need to assure the rest of the world

00:10:12.608 --> 00:10:17.071
that they are really seriously
and sincerely working together

00:10:17.071 --> 00:10:20.700
to find their alternative
and to rebuild partnership.

00:10:21.951 --> 00:10:23.786
One thing to keep in mind:

00:10:23.786 --> 00:10:27.957
the climate change doesn't care
about our ideological divide.

00:10:27.957 --> 00:10:34.046
Rather, it demands for collective actions
that deliver outcomes.

00:10:34.088 --> 00:10:37.383
Cornering China
as a national security threat

00:10:37.425 --> 00:10:40.678
seems to claim that the US,
rather than China,

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:46.309
is the legitimate and trustworthy
global leader in this transition.

00:10:46.350 --> 00:10:50.146
And yet, as the world's largest
developed economy,

00:10:50.188 --> 00:10:54.609
the US doesn't meet the bar
of what's expected of a global leader.

00:10:55.818 --> 00:11:00.490
Along the line, it doesn't provide
the rest of the world

00:11:00.490 --> 00:11:05.453
with sufficient, accessible
and affordable clean energy solutions,

00:11:05.453 --> 00:11:09.582
nor does it provide, deliver
its financial commitments

00:11:09.582 --> 00:11:12.919
to other developing countries
under the Paris Agreement.

00:11:15.588 --> 00:11:20.551
And China undoubtedly
has to go a long way too

00:11:20.593 --> 00:11:25.097
in rethinking its strategy and behavior
in dealing with the US.

00:11:25.139 --> 00:11:28.267
It needs to make extra efforts
to convince the world

00:11:28.309 --> 00:11:32.021
that it's not a threat,
but rather a trusted partner,

00:11:32.063 --> 00:11:35.233
willing and capable to work with the US

00:11:35.274 --> 00:11:38.361
to shift towards
a collaborative partnership.

00:11:39.570 --> 00:11:44.367
Let me leave this stage
with some sort of cautious optimism.

00:11:44.367 --> 00:11:48.246
My heart feels enlightened
when media in our two countries

00:11:48.246 --> 00:11:50.957
start to tell different US-China stories.

00:11:52.083 --> 00:11:55.711
Treasury Secretary Yellen's
China trip last week

00:11:55.753 --> 00:11:58.422
went viral in Chinese social media.

00:12:00.216 --> 00:12:03.928
The rainbow welcoming
her landing in Beijing Airport

00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:06.222
represents some hope

00:12:06.264 --> 00:12:09.725
and also a new beginning
of bilateral relations.

00:12:10.476 --> 00:12:15.064
And her love for the wild mushroom
soup from Yunnan province --

00:12:15.106 --> 00:12:16.232
(Laughter)

00:12:16.274 --> 00:12:21.654
literally gives me this kind of a warm
and also sweet human touch.

00:12:23.114 --> 00:12:27.702
And I have a message
to climate envoy John Kerry,

00:12:27.702 --> 00:12:29.912
who is coming to China later this month.

00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:37.336
You know, the two governments
have already declared quite a number

00:12:37.378 --> 00:12:40.965
of joint commitments
and collective actions

00:12:41.007 --> 00:12:43.342
to fight climate change.

00:12:43.384 --> 00:12:48.848
What's urgently needed now
is a shared vision, mission, aspiration,

00:12:48.889 --> 00:12:51.350
wisdom and very importantly,

00:12:51.392 --> 00:12:54.979
a compass to guide everyone back on track,

00:12:55.021 --> 00:12:59.483
to take collective actions
and deliver the due results.

00:12:59.483 --> 00:13:04.780
It seems to me that's
the must-have precondition for us all

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:08.909
in order to keep
a sustainable future within reach.

00:13:08.909 --> 00:13:10.202
Thank you.

00:13:10.202 --> 00:13:13.873
(Applause)

